            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e122-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysms, characterized by abnormal dilatations of a localized portion of the coronary artery, are an uncommon finding during angiography. We present a case where a giant right coronary aneurysm was detected during angiography, in a patient admitted with a inferior wall myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
